joe Linux: anonymous mappings are not named, as glibc does not name them by default. Naming is a
prctl() call at every mapping, malloc's included, which the seccomp filters of programs written for
glibc do not allow: dhcpcd's killed it at the first malloc() that mapped memory, and OpenSSH's
sandbox allows no prctl() either. __bionic_set_vma_name names nothing; scudo's and GWP-ASan's
names are dropped in their 0002 patches.

diff --git i/libc/platform/bionic/vma_name.h w/libc/platform/bionic/vma_name.h
index 8df97d7..fd53bc1 100644
--- i/libc/platform/bionic/vma_name.h
+++ w/libc/platform/bionic/vma_name.h
@@ -27,20 +27,21 @@
 #include <sys/prctl.h>
 
 /*
- * joe Linux: names an anonymous mapping, for /proc/PID/maps and crash reports.
+ * joe Linux: where Android names an anonymous mapping (for /proc/PID/maps and
+ * crash reports), joe Linux does not, as glibc does not (unless its
+ * glibc.mem.decorate_maps tunable is set).
  *
- * Naming needs a kernel built with CONFIG_ANON_VMA_NAME. Android's kernels are;
- * many Linux kernels are not, and there every name is refused with EINVAL. A
- * name is only an aid to debugging, and the functions that map memory (malloc,
- * atexit, dlopen, thread creation, ...) must not leave that error in errno when
- * they succeed: programs written for glibc read errno after calls that set it
- * only on failure (the kernel's kallsyms does after getline at the end of a
- * file). So errno is left as it was, and the error is returned: 0 when the
- * mapping is named.
+ * Naming is a prctl() call at every mapping, malloc's included, and the
+ * seccomp filters of programs written for glibc do not allow prctl():
+ * dhcpcd's killed it at the first malloc() that mapped memory, and OpenSSH's
+ * sandbox allows no prctl() either. It also needs a kernel built with
+ * CONFIG_ANON_VMA_NAME, which many Linux kernels are not. The call sites
+ * keep the names Android gives; this returns 0 as if the mapping had been
+ * named, and leaves errno alone.
  */
 static inline int __bionic_set_vma_name(const void* addr, size_t size, const char* name) {
-  int saved_errno = errno;
-  int error = prctl(PR_SET_VMA, PR_SET_VMA_ANON_NAME, addr, size, name) == 0 ? 0 : errno;
-  errno = saved_errno;
-  return error;
+  (void)addr;
+  (void)size;
+  (void)name;
+  return 0;
 }
